WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.356
Traceglass follows the real source of saved n8n workflow output.

2
00:00:05.376 --> 00:00:15.744
A parent and child can both finish successfully, with matching
business JSON, while the saved parent pairing points to a different
customer.

3
00:00:15.764 --> 00:00:18.576
This is a recorded synthetic example.

4
00:00:18.576 --> 00:00:21.007
Select terminal item one.

5
00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:26.582
The cyan path traces back through child ancestry to caller input two.

6
00:00:26.602 --> 00:00:29.719
The dashed red path records input one.

7
00:00:29.739 --> 00:00:35.688
The inspector shows the exact saved pairedItem values and their JSON
pointers.

8
00:00:35.688 --> 00:00:39.691
The evidence agent sees that same selected item.

9
00:00:39.711 --> 00:00:42.425
We ask it to compare the repair.

10
00:00:42.445 --> 00:00:46.181
It calls the native focus and audit actions.

11
00:00:46.201 --> 00:00:50.856
The human workbench moves to the repaired case as the agent works.

12
00:00:50.856 --> 00:00:55.110
The repaired call has matching recorded and derived roots.

13
00:00:55.130 --> 00:01:03.198
The agent gives a short release conclusion, with its real tool inputs
and outputs available for inspection.

14
00:01:03.218 --> 00:01:09.528
These actions are also shared with the native CLI and HTTP API.

15
00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:12.060
Download a release dossier.

16
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:18.411
It includes the selected finding and raw evidence, without rewriting
either export.

17
00:01:18.431 --> 00:01:25.488
Missing child runData produces an incomplete-evidence state and a
request for the full child export.

18
00:01:25.488 --> 00:01:32.168
Traceglass adds a purpose-built human-agent workbench to our existing
open-source audit.

19
00:01:32.188 --> 00:01:39.808
The live example uses synthetic customers; private exports belong in a
self-hosted workspace.

20
00:01:39.828 --> 00:01:42.024
Source and setup are public.
